# Versions are exact-pinned (==X.Y.Z) so OSV-Scanner can resolve a single
# concrete version per line. Wildcards (==X.*) prevented the scanner from
# matching the actual installed version and produced false-positive CVE
# reports across the major series. Dependabot's weekly minor/patch group
# (see .github/dependabot.yml) keeps these moving.
Flask==3.1.3
firebase-admin==7.7.0
flask-wtf==1.3.0
flask-limiter==4.1.1
gunicorn==26.2.0
google-cloud-firestore==2.34.1
google-cloud-storage==3.17.1
google-cloud-secret-manager==2.31.0
google-cloud-logging==3.17.0
# Portail client (spec L1): the portal enqueues events onto the « portail »
# Cloud Tasks queue; the main service's handler consumes them. Reused as-is
# by the future phase J notification pipeline.
google-cloud-tasks==2.26.0
# requests was already in the hash lock as a locked transitive (cachecontrol,
# google-api-core, ...). utils/graph.py (Microsoft Graph outbound email) now
# imports it directly, so it is promoted to a direct pin — Dependabot and
# OSV-Scanner track direct deps only.
requests==2.34.2
# OpenTelemetry — distributed tracing → Cloud Trace via the OTLP endpoint.
# Versions are PAIRED and must move together: the stable line (api/sdk 1.45.2)
# ships alongside the beta contrib line (instrumentation 0.66b2), and each
# instrumentation package hard-pins its siblings at `==0.66b2`. Bumping one
# alone is unresolvable — this is a single atomic edit, and Dependabot cannot
# automate it: its minor/patch group leaves out pins that only resolve
# together.
# 1.44.0 -> 1.45.2 (2026-11-05) fixes the medium CVE-2026-114603
# (GHSA-xcq7-p3pf-p88h): TraceState.from_header ran a quadratic regex over
# the inbound W3C `tracestate`, with no length check first. Reachable: the
# W3C propagator that tracing_setup installs parses it on both services
# before any auth guard, on every request outside EXCLUDED_URLS that carries
# a valid traceparent. gunicorn's 8190-byte header line bounded one value
# (some 50-70 ms of CPU on 1.44.0, measured locally), but gunicorn joins
# repeated lines into one value: the ~15 that fit under Cloudflare's 128 KB
# request-header cap could hold the GIL for 0.7-1 s. Since 1.45.1 the parse
# is linear and a value over 8192 characters is dropped with one fixed-text
# WARNING (the traceparent is still honoured); 1.45.2 also ignores a
# `traceparent` over 512 characters, with a WARNING too, and its sdk is the
# patch paired with contrib 0.66b2.
# Since 1.45.0, span attributes keep mappings and nested sequences, which
# 1.44.0 dropped, bytes, which it decoded to str, and any other type as its
# str(), which it dropped. utils/tracing_setup.py now scrubs inside all of
# them and its guard drops the str()-ed kind (OBSERVABILITY.md, « PII
# controls in traces »), but mapping KEYS are exported verbatim. Every call
# site sets scalars today: keep it so.
opentelemetry-api==1.45.2
opentelemetry-sdk==1.45.2
# Export goes to telemetry.googleapis.com over OTLP/gRPC (2026-07-30, replacing
# the deprecated opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace). gRPC and not HTTP because
# only the gRPC exporter takes `credentials=`, which is the ONLY auth path that
# refreshes the token per RPC — `headers=` is frozen at construction, so a
# Bearer token there would expire in ~1 h and UNAUTHENTICATED is not a
# retryable code: traces would stop while the app kept serving. grpcio is
# already required by ten other packages (Firestore, Logging, Secret Manager,
# Cloud Tasks…), so this adds no native weight.
# 1.45.2 brings one new transitive, opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-common 0.66b2:
# the exporter's self-metrics module moved there from -proto-common. Pure
# Python, Apache-2.0, requiring only opentelemetry-sdk; a no-op unless
# OTEL_PYTHON_SDK_INTERNAL_METRICS_ENABLED is "true" (any case, blanks
# stripped), which nothing here sets.
opentelemetry-exporter-otlp-proto-grpc==1.45.2
# Three upstream-maintained lines producing exactly MIGRATION.md's
# composite_channel_credentials(ssl, metadata_call_credentials(AuthMetadataPlugin))
# pattern. Beta, but trivially inlinable into tracing_setup.py if it ever
# stalls. All of its deps (grpcio, google-auth, requests) are already locked.
opentelemetry-exporter-credential-provider-gcp==0.66b2
# NOT deprecated and NOT part of the exporter family — this is the
# X-Cloud-Trace-Context propagator, which the OTLP migration leaves untouched.
opentelemetry-propagator-gcp==1.15.0
opentelemetry-instrumentation-flask==0.66b2
opentelemetry-instrumentation-requests==0.66b2
opentelemetry-instrumentation-jinja2==0.66b2
# Was transitive via the (now removed) GCP exporter; kept as a direct pin
