reportlab==5.1.0
# Pillow is a transitive dependency of reportlab (which only requires >=9.0.0).
# Pinned explicitly here for CVE hygiene. 12.3.0 -> 13.0.0 (2026-11-05)
# closes the 41 GitHub advisories open against 12.3.0, and two more that
# Pillow has published but GitHub has not yet imported (GHSA-xcvg-w56q-r89m,
# GHSA-wqgw-9xfh-qf2g). Five are critical by GitHub's rating (Pillow's own
# rates two): CVE-2026-112398 (FlashPix JPEG tiles), CVE-2026-96639
# (multi-frame loaders reusing stale storage), CVE-2026-112403 (scaled
# decode of a lossless JPEG), CVE-2026-112393 (a TIFF saved to a BytesIO)
# and CVE-2026-112900 (an EPS file name injected into the Ghostscript
# command line). The 36 others, high or medium by GitHub, are decoder
# overflows and out-of-bounds reads, decompression-bomb bypasses, endless or
# quadratic parses and encoder memory errors across Pillow's formats and its
# PdfParser, plus memory errors in image operations (merge, transform,
# quantize, rank filters, ImageMorph), font rendering (FreeType, PILfont)
# and Arrow export.
# None is reachable: each needs the app to call Pillow itself — to open,
# save or transform an image, render text or append to a PDF — and nothing
# does. No Athena module imports PIL, but reportlab does at import
# (reportlab/lib/utils.py), and so does pypdf (pypdf/_page.py, when Pillow
# is installed), so PIL.Image loads in a worker that builds a PDF or serves
# any connector call (mcp/handlers.py imports utils/pdf_text.py) — yet no
# image plugin ever registers. The builders (utils/*_pdf.py) draw text
# tables only — no drawImage, ImageReader, Image flowable or logo — and
# escape() every user string before Paragraph markup, so a typed
# `<img src=...>` prints as text instead of reaching Image.open; pypdf's
# extract_text() skips images, and get_document_text refuses image files
# before any download.
# 13.0.0 is a major release: its removals (Image._show,
# ImageCmsProfile.product_name/product_info, ...) and the move of
# get_child_images from Image to ImageFile touch no API reportlab 5.1.0 or
# pypdf calls, and the PDF tests pass unchanged.
Pillow==13.0.0
# Markdown renders every note: on screen through main.py's `markdown`
# filter, and into Word for note prints and the connector's Markdown
# through utils/markdown_docx.py, bleach after it both ways. 3.11 -> 3.11.2
# (2026-11-06) is NOT byte-identical: of 23,953 inputs (the 1,476 the tests
# render, all unchanged; every string literal in tests/; upstream's test
# inputs; synthetic notes), 194 render differently on screen and 193 in
# Word, each traced to 3.11.1. Text that 3.11 dropped now shows: everything
# after an unterminated end tag (`</foo`), and the text of an element whose
# quoted attribute holds `>`. Emphasis was rewritten (#1632; 3.11.2
# reverted its CommonMark punctuation rules, #1657): nesting now holds
# (`*a **b** c*` was three italics), but a closing run after a space no
# longer closes, so `**Faits : **texte` now shows its asterisks, as does a
# mismatched run (`**mot*`); and `**` nested 32 deep no longer converts to
# Word (the connector refuses it, a note print falls back to the raw text).
# 3.11.2 -> 3.11.3 (2026-11-06): of the same inputs, 169 render differently,
# 150 of them the tests' generated fence-and-backtick strings (no test
# asserts their output). Mismatched backtick runs pair anew, so the text
# 3.11.2 lost between them shows (`a `b`` c` rendered "a <code></code> c"),
# a link-reference definition followed by `===` no longer becomes a heading,
# and long emphasis chains close as written (#1690). Unchanged: the link
# schemes bleach lets through (the new `<scheme:...>` autolinks gain
# nothing), and every Word fragment is well-formed. And the quadratic
# parses are gone: a 100,000-character note of `#` then text renders in
# 16 ms instead of 2 minutes, 5,000 reference definitions in 12 ms instead
# of 12 s.
Markdown==3.11.3
# bleach is archived upstream; 6.4.0 is a security release clearing the
# URI-scheme sanitization advisories (GHSA-gj48-438w-jh9v, GHSA-8rfp-98v4-mmr6)
# and moving off the 6.3.0-only linkify email-DoS advisory (GHSA-g75f-g53v-794x).
# Longer term, migrate note sanitization to nh3 (maintained successor) to exit
# this recurring class of unpatched bleach alerts.
bleach==6.4.0
