# all arrive via the google/firebase client stack. cryptography 50.0.0 clears
# the 2026-08 batch — CVE-2026-69247 (PKCS#7 EnvelopedData Bleichenbacher
# oracle, fixed 50.0.0), CVE-2026-69249 (exponential X.509 path-building) and
# CVE-2026-69248 (wildcard-SAN escape from permittedSubtrees), both fixed
# 49.0.0 — on top of the earlier bundled-OpenSSL patch (GHSA-537c-gmf6-5ccf).
# None was reachable here (the app never decrypts PKCS#7 nor builds X.509
# chains with cryptography's verifier — it only verifies Firebase JWT
# signatures), so these are hygiene bumps. msgpack 1.2.1 fixes an Unpacker
# out-of-bounds read after a caught error (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964). h2 4.4.1
# fixes CVE-2026-71554 (duplicate Host header forwarded on HTTP/2→1.1
# downgrade — a request-smuggling primitive for SERVERS; here h2 is only
# httpx's outbound HTTP/2 client via firebase-admin, so equally unreachable).
cryptography==50.0.2
