h2==4.4.1
# pyjwt arrives only via firebase-admin, and only its App Check verifier runs
# it here (firebase_admin.app_check: alg pinned to RS256, jwt.decode with
# algorithms=["RS256"]). 2.13.0 carried ten advisories (2026-09-29). The one
# REACHABLE here was CVE-2026-101917 (GHSA-2gx3-rcp4-g85q): PyJWKClient
# re-fetched the JWKS on every unknown `kid`, and the kid is read from the
# UNVERIFIED token header, so any unauthenticated request carrying a forged
# X-Firebase-AppCheck header forced one outbound HTTPS fetch — on the main
# service (HX-Request is attacker-settable) and on the public portal. Every
# such request still ended in a 401. 2.14.0+ adds a refetch cooldown and a
# per-client lock around the fetch; note the cooldown starts only after a
# SUCCESSFUL fetch, so while Google's JWKS endpoint is failing each forged kid
# still costs one fetch, now serialized. The HS/asymmetric algorithm-confusion
# advisories (CVE-2026-102268 — labelled critical — -102271, -102272, -102273)
# and the empty-HMAC-JWK one (-102266) need an HS* algorithm in the allow-list
# and are unreachable under RS256-only; -102267 (JWKS redirects) and -102274
# (malformed RSA JWK) need an attacker-controlled response from Google's
# hard-coded JWKS URL; -102269 (non-canonical signature) needs raw-token
# revocation state, which nothing keeps; -102265 (RecursionError on a deeply
# nested header) ends in the verifiers' `except Exception` → 401. 2.15.1
# carries every 2.14.0 fix, caches the parsed key set, and reverts 2.14.0's
# over-strict `=` padding rejection. firebase-admin 7.4.0 requires
# pyjwt[crypto]>=2.10.1 with no upper bound. tests/test_appcheck_pyjwt.py runs
# the real verifier against this pin.
pyjwt==2.15.1
# anyio arrives only via httpx ← firebase-admin (httpx[http2]==0.28.1). 4.14.2
# fixes CVE-2026-63374 (GHSA-82r6-8w77-94w6 — IDNA-2003 host-name encoding in
# TLSStream/connect_tcp enabling certificate spoofing for NON-ASCII hosts) and
# CVE-2026-64847 (GHSA-5p39-cfhj-2xmp — process-pool workers deadlocking on
# undrained stderr). Neither is reachable: importing the whole default app and
# the portal loads httpx but never httpcore or anyio (the only httpx client
# firebase-admin builds is FCM messaging's, which the app never imports), every
# host the app contacts is ASCII, and nothing uses anyio process pools. A
# hygiene bump.
anyio==4.16.0
